# Allowed sites of each structure pattern, per file. A line is `ROW KIND COUNT FILE`; KIND is
# `prod`, or `test` for tests/ directories, tests.rs and *_tests.rs. structure-check fails when a
# file has more sites than its line allows (none without a line), and when it has fewer: lower the
# line to the new count and delete it at 0. Counts only fall: `check --changed` also fails when a
# count is above the one the allowlist at the base revision holds, so a rise is the lead's act on main.
# Every row scans crates/ and apps/.
#
# crate_fields:       struct fields (named or tuple) declared pub(crate), pub(super) or pub(in ..), in
#                     crates/*/src and apps/*/src: internal state visible past its module. Fields
#                     that a macro generates are not counted.
# pub_fields:         struct fields declared pub, of a struct of any visibility, in the same
#                     sources: each such type states its contract. Fields that a macro generates
#                     are not counted.
# xmin_xmax:          `.xmin` and `.xmax` text outside crates/adtb/src/mvcc. Destructuring and struct
#                     literals are not counted. The row ends when the fields become private
#                     (ticket structure-version-owner).
# disallowed_methods: mentions of clippy::disallowed_methods in an expect or allow attribute. The
#                     lint rejects storage::page::owner, pages::Exclusive::write,
#                     PageMemory::lock_exclusive, PageMemory::try_lock_exclusive and
#                     Optimistic::upgrade (clippy.toml); each allowed site carries an expect, or its
#                     file one inner expect where the file owns the item.
# crash_loops:        definitions of a function whose name holds `crash_loop`: the harness's one
#                     crash loop, which runs the ledger check after every round.
# crash_allows:       definitions of `fn allows`: what a crash loop's reopened database tolerates.
# sim_test_opens:     in crates/adtb-sim/tests, by name: a function taking parameters whose name
#                     begins with `open`, `opened`, `opens`, `opening` or a `reopen` form, or ends
#                     with `_open`, `_opened`, `_opens` or a `_reopen` form; a closure bound to
#                     `open`, `opened`, `opens`, `opening` or a `reopen` form; and `fn engine` whose
#                     body begins with `Engine::open`. A test opens through adtb_simkit::open or
#                     fixture::Storage, or calls `Database::open_in` in its own body. The lines
#                     left are local open helpers and helpers whose names only mention an open.
# sim_test_damage:    definitions of `fn flip`, `zeroed`, `damage` or `damaged_part` in
#                     crates/adtb-sim/tests: byte damage goes through adtb_harness::damage.
# sim_test_offsets:   in crates/adtb-sim/tests, a product with a page size (`PAGE`, `*_PAGE`,
#                     `PAGE_SIZE`, `page_size`, `8192`, `4096`), or `.get_mut(NAME)` /
#                     `.get_mut(FILE)` on a device's files: a page's bytes come from
#                     adtb_harness::damage::DataFile. The lines left count sizes, not offsets.
# crash_loops, crash_allows, sim_test_opens and sim_test_damage count names: a helper under
#                     another name escapes them. sim_test_offsets counts spellings of arithmetic.
